Leo: How about planting trees on the hill behind the school?
Mia: I like that. Trees take in carbon dioxide and give us fresh air.
Leo: Exactly. And the hill looks so bare and grey now.
Mia: How many trees do you think we could plant?
Leo: If everyone helps, maybe a hundred young trees in one day.
Mia: Wonderful. I''ll ask the teacher to choose a good weekend.
Leo: Great. Let''s make a poster to get more students to join.', 'Mia 说班级本学期需要一个环保项目;Leo 提议在学校后山种树;Mia 赞同,树能吸收二氧化碳、提供新鲜空气;后山现在光秃秃的;若大家帮忙,一天能种约一百棵小树;Mia 去请老师定周末;Leo 提议做海报吸引更多同学参加。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the class need this term?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A green project.","A sports match.","A new classroom.","A music show."]},{"q":"What does Leo suggest doing?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cleaning the canteen.","Planting trees behind the school.","Selling old books.","Building a new hill."]},{"q":"Why are trees good, according to Mia?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They take in carbon dioxide and give fresh air.","They make the hill look grey.","They need no water at all.","They block the sunlight."]},{"q":"How many trees might they plant in one day?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only two or three.","About a hundred.","Exactly one thousand.","None at all."]},{"q":"What will Leo do to get more students to join?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Cancel the project.","Cut down the trees.","Make a poster.","Stay at home."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U4', 'sufe');
One main cause is the greenhouse effect from gases like carbon dioxide.
As the planet warms, the polar ice begins to melt.
When the ice melts, the level of the sea rises.
Scientists warn that extreme weather may also happen more often.', '地球正逐年缓慢变暖;一个主要原因是二氧化碳等气体造成的温室效应;随着地球变暖,极地冰开始融化;冰融化时,海平面上升;科学家警告极端天气也可能更频繁地发生。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is happening to the Earth year after year?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It is getting much colder.","It is staying exactly the same.","It is moving away from the sun.","It is slowly getting warmer."]},{"q":"What is one main cause of the warming?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The greenhouse effect from gases like carbon dioxide.","Too much rain in winter.","The light of the moon.","People planting trees."]},{"q":"What begins to happen to the polar ice?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It grows much thicker.","It begins to melt.","It turns into rock.","It stays frozen forever."]},{"q":"What does the melting ice do to the sea?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It makes the sea disappear.","It makes the sea colder only.","It makes the sea level rise.","It has no effect on the sea."]},{"q":"What else may happen more often, scientists warn?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Longer school holidays.","Cheaper electricity.","Quieter cities.","Extreme weather."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U4', 'sufe');
Sam: Of course. Too much rubbish ends up on this beach and harms the animals.
Reporter: What kind of rubbish do you usually find?
Sam: Mostly plastic — bottles, bags and bits of packaging.
Reporter: How many people have come today?
Sam: More than two hundred volunteers, and new ones keep arriving.
Reporter: That''s amazing. What do you hope people will learn?
Sam: I hope they will simply use less plastic in their daily lives.', '记者问 Sam 为何组织这次清理;Sam 说太多垃圾留在海滩、伤害动物;通常捡到的多是塑料——瓶子、袋子和包装碎片;今天来了两百多名志愿者,还有人不断到来;Sam 希望大家在日常生活中少用塑料。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Sam organise the clean-up?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Too much rubbish on the beach harms the animals.","He wants to sell the rubbish.","He likes swimming in winter.","The beach is too quiet."]},{"q":"What kind of rubbish does Sam usually find?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Mostly glass.","Mostly plastic.","Mostly metal.","Mostly wood."]},{"q":"How many volunteers have come today?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only about ten.","Exactly fifty.","More than two hundred.","None so far."]},{"q":"What are new volunteers still doing?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Going back home.","Refusing to help.","Selling bottles.","Arriving at the beach."]},{"q":"What does Sam hope people will learn?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To use less plastic in daily life.","To visit the beach less often.","To buy more bottles.","To stop cleaning beaches."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U4', 'sufe');
First, take a bus or ride a bike instead of going by car.
Second, turn off the lights and unplug devices you are not using.
Third, choose local food and products with less packaging.
None of these steps is hard, but together they really help the planet.', '这里有几个让碳足迹变小的简单方法:第一,坐公交或骑自行车,而不是开车;第二,关灯并拔掉不用的电器;第三,选择本地食物和包装少的产品;每一步都不难,但合在一起真的能帮助地球。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the talk mainly about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["How to grow more food at home.","Easy ways to make your carbon footprint smaller.","Why cars are fun to drive.","How to win a sports match."]},{"q":"What is the first suggestion?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Buy a bigger car.","Travel only by plane.","Take a bus or ride a bike instead of driving.","Stay in bed all day."]},{"q":"What should you do with devices you are not using?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Leave them all switched on.","Throw them into the sea.","Sell them to friends.","Turn off the lights and unplug them."]},{"q":"What kind of products should you choose?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Local food with less packaging.","Food shipped from far away.","Products with heavy packaging.","Things you do not need."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about these steps?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Each one is very expensive.","None is hard, but together they really help.","They make no difference at all.","Only experts can do them."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U4', 'sufe');
Anna: I understand, but I try to stay optimistic about it.
Ben: How can you? The ice is melting and the sea is rising.
Anna: True, yet more and more people are starting to act.
Ben: Do you really think ordinary people can change anything?
Anna: Yes. When millions make small green choices, the result is huge.
Ben: I suppose you''re right. Being pessimistic helps no one.
Anna: Exactly. Hope gives us the energy to keep trying.', 'Ben 觉得地球真的有麻烦;Anna 理解但努力保持乐观;Ben 不解,冰在融化、海在上升;Anna 说越来越多人开始行动;Ben 怀疑普通人能否改变什么;Anna 说当数百万人做小的绿色选择,结果是巨大的;Ben 认同,悲观对谁都没帮助;Anna 说希望给我们坚持的动力。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How does Anna try to feel about the Earth?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She feels totally hopeless.","She does not care at all.","She tries to stay optimistic.","She is always angry."]},{"q":"What worries Ben?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The weather is too cold.","There are too many trees.","People act too quickly.","The ice is melting and the sea is rising."]},{"q":"What does Anna say is happening with people?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["More and more of them are starting to act.","They are all giving up.","They never think about it.","They are leaving the cities."]},{"q":"What happens when millions make small green choices?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Nothing changes.","The result is huge.","The Earth gets colder.","The choices are wasted."]},{"q":"What does Ben finally agree about being pessimistic?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It solves everything.","It is the only choice.","It helps no one.","It saves energy."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U4', 'sufe');
You do not have to be a scientist to make a difference.
Sort your rubbish, save water, and walk for short trips.
Speak up and ask your school and town to go greener.
Remember, it is everyone working together that can save our Earth.', '年轻人,地球的未来部分掌握在你们手中;你不必是科学家也能带来改变;给垃圾分类、节约用水、短途步行;勇敢发声,要求学校和城镇更环保;记住,正是大家齐心协力才能拯救地球。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Whose hands is the planet''s future partly in?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only scientists''.","Only leaders''.","No one''s.","Young people''s."]},{"q":"Do you need to be a scientist to make a difference?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["No, you do not.","Yes, you must be one.","Only if you are old.","Only on weekends."]},{"q":"Which action does the speaker suggest?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy more plastic bags.","Sort your rubbish and save water.","Leave the taps running.","Drive everywhere alone."]},{"q":"What should young people ask their school and town to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To build more factories.","To use more energy.","To go greener.","To stop recycling."]},{"q":"According to the speaker, what can save the Earth?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["One person alone.","Doing nothing at all.","Waiting for the future.","Everyone working together."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U4', 'sufe');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='sufe' AND volume='elective3' AND unit='U4';

I am writing on behalf of the Green Club to call on everyone to go green. As you may have noticed, our campus produces far too much waste every day, and most of the plastic and paper is simply thrown away. This not only wastes resources but also harms the environment around us.

To deal with this, our school can place clearly marked bins so that we can sort our rubbish. We students can also carry reusable bags and turn off the lights when we leave a room. In this way, less waste will end up in nature.

None of these steps is hard. It is all of us, working together, that can make a real difference. Let''s act today!

Yours,
Li Hua', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["I am writing on behalf of the Green Club to call on everyone to go green.","Most of the plastic and paper is simply thrown away, which harms the environment.","Our school can place clearly marked bins so that we can sort our rubbish.","It is all of us, working together, that can make a real difference."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"It is all of us who makes a difference.","correct":"It is all of us who make a difference.","note":"强调句强调复数 us,后面动词用 make,主谓一致看被强调的真实主语。"},{"wrong":"Our campus produce too much waste.","correct":"Our campus produces too much waste.","note":"主语 campus 第三人称单数,动词加 s。"},{"wrong":"It was in 2020 when the city banned plastic bags.","correct":"It was in 2020 that the city banned plastic bags.","note":"强调时间状语时连接词用 that,不用 when。"}]'::jsonb, '【环保倡议信结构】
称呼:Dear schoolmates,
第1段 目的:I am writing … to call on everyone to go green.
第2段 问题+后果:One serious problem is … This harms …
第3段 办法+效果:Our school can … We students can also … In this way, …
第4段 号召(强调句):It is all of us that … Let''s act today!
落款:Yours, Li Hua', 2, 'elective3', 'U4', 'sufe');

